{
  "comment": [
    "Benchmark workload matrix (redesign section 4.5, second bullet):",
    "which cells of (world extent x chunk extent x layout x storage x",
    "executor x payload) the benchmark suite measures, derived from",
    "registration names through fail-closed family grammars plus",
    "curated defaults/overrides for what names cannot express, checked",
    "by tools/check_workload_matrix.py (hooks tier + bench job).",
    "Extents with depth 1 omit the trailing x1 (512x512 means",
    "512x512x1). Scenario-layer cells (section 3.1) join in phase 3.",
    "storage=always_resident means an AlwaysResidentWorld: names",
    "containing 'sparse' usually mean sparse BLOCKERS (a layout);",
    "maintenance/sparse|dense is a task-scheduling pattern (payload).",
    "Only residency/* and the one sparse_resident batch planner use",
    "sparse storage.",
    "The portal batch registrations stay non-composite: each measures one uniform configuration (room_portals, shared goal), unlike the mixed-goal batch families marked composite."
  ],
  "vocabularies": {
    "storage": [
      "always_resident",
      "sparse_resident",
      "not_applicable"
    ],
    "executor_kind": [
      "serial",
      "pool",
      "scoped_threads"
    ],
    "layout": [
      "open",
      "room_portals",
      "sparse_blockers",
      "axis_detour",
      "striped_maze",
      "wall_gap",
      "branch_lattice",
      "single_blocker",
      "sealed",
      "slab_gap",
      "slab_multi_gap",
      "corridor_3d",
      "carved_lanes",
      "construction_stripe",
      "not_applicable"
    ]
  },
  "families": [
